Today, Saturday 26th August 2006, at 19:10 GMT+1

marnie-Val-Hum-Fem-Law ascended to demigoddess-hood!

I've been playing NetHack for nearly two years, and finally I've
managed to do it.
I guess now I have to narrate marnie's story, but I must confess I've
never been good at writing.
So... I'll just try.

The first few levels went smooth, I decided to take the Gnomish Mines
immediately and got to Minetown with no problem. I would have liked to
exploit the protection racket, but I simply couldn't avoid fighting
after my kitten died on level 2. Let's check the altar... neutral...
ok, better luck next time! For the moment let's equip ourselves with
dwarven mithril and get our AC below zero. I headed for Mines' End (the
Catacombs) and took my luckstone. Then, during my journey to the
Sokoban, I found a bag of holding! This proved very useful, even if I
started with high strength, but the lack of a mean to bless it soon
became annoying... and this is also because in the mines I had
price-identified two uncursed magic lamps! In Sokoban I luckily found
its right complement, the Amulet of reflection.
While there, I made a mistake, because I ate a gremlin and acquired
teleportitis. Later I had to kill some tengus to get teleport control,
too, which eventually came up handy.
Then I started strolling down and down... an altar! Is it lawful? Nope,
Loki's... Let's proceed. Some levels down, again, an altar! But Loki's.
Another altar! Odin's... Tyr, where are you!? I even found another
altar but, again, it was Loki's. Can you believe that? Five altars,
three of which actually where temples with a priest, and none of them
was lawful. Meanwhile I cleared up Fort Ludios and killed Medusa (I had
a ring of levitation to get there). I desperately had to convert an
altar, so I started reading scrolls of create monster until a gray
unicorn came up... all right, the altar on this level is chaotic, let's
do it! After converting, I could finally obtain holy water to bless the
bag and the lamps. One of these simply freed a peaceful djinni, but
with the other I wished for a blessed +2 GDSM. I started sacrificing to
get Mjollnir, then I went for the Quest.
All those giants easily took marnie's strength up to 18/**, and she
smashed down Lord Surtur in just two turns of melee. Before descendeing
below Medusa, she found around several nurses and incubi that helped
her to arrive to level 30 (sic) with over 500 HP. Further sacrificing
only yielded a bunch of crap artifacts: Ogresmasher, Trollsbane,
Demonsbane... I preferred sticking to the +7 Excalibur, the +6 Mjollnir
and a +6 silver saber in the other hand. I set up a stash in Fort
Ludios and started polypiling, which earned 4 scrolls of genocide (used
immediately for liches, mind flayers and disenchanters), speed boots
and a robe. And what a surprise when I discovered that this took most
of marnie's spell failure rates to 0%... so not too bad she had lost
her cloak of displacement after eating a chameleon and turning into a
gray dragon! Other very useful things I had already found include a
ring of slow digestion (I love this one) and one of free action; I also
had a ring of conflict, but I never needed to use it.
So, after enchanting all the stuff and getting to AC -38, I went down
and
laid waste the Castle. In the Valley of the Dead and later in Gehennom
I found two more magic lamps (how lucky!) and used the wishes for
gauntlets of dexterity (I know this is unusual for a Valkyrie, but I
had really good spellcasting, including the terribly-useful identify)
and a spellbook of cone of cold (just another attack spell since I
already had force bolt and magic missile, but... well, I hate water,
and moreover I think that a spellcasting Valkyrie without this spell
definitely has something wrong). I could also use 3 more wishes from
the wand I found in the Castle, but what could I ask? So I just kept it
in my bag of holding, in case of necessity (that did not come up).
In the Valley a green slime touched me and I started panicking, mainly
because that was the first slime I had ever encountered and I was in a
cul-de-sac. So I invoked the Orb of Fate, teleported to level 20 and
prayed. This simply hit the spot, but for a few turns I had been nearly
paralyzed for the terror of an incumbent death by sliming. So I
eventually genocided green slimes :).
Alright. Asmodeus, Juiblex, Baalzebub, Vlad and Orcus went down without
any problem. I reached the bottom of the dungeon, found the Vibrating
Square, left there the Bell and the Candelabrum with the candles I
bought from Izchak and entered Rodney's Tower. He went down without
problems, too. I performed the Invocation, killed the high priest of
Moloch, took the Amulet and started my first ascension run (I never
managed to go past the Castle before, so what a big leap!)
The run proved easy indeed, because marnie was physically nearly
invulnerable and had already cleared the paths with her trusty
pick-axe.
Plane of Earth... this was Rodney's last apparition, the fourth (from
what I have read on this group it seems four is a very little number).
Taking down him and his friends was elementary. Plane of Air... Fire...
Water... well, I got scared in this one because I was afraid of being
let out of the air bubble, but this didn't happen even when water
elementals surrounded me and I couldn't move. So... the first four
planes were just too easy. The Astral Plane is quite another matter. I
had a wand of death with 7 charges to deal with Famine and Pestilence,
but I was very afraid of Death. She stood in the left branch, while
Famine was in the centre and Pestilence to the right. So I started from
Pestilence, but the altar was neutral. I had to come back (I had to
kill Pestilence thrice) and checked Famine's altar, only to discover
that it was chaotic (and I had to kill Famine twice). This was the
truth... I had to deal with Death. She came out of her room on her own
initiative, and to my great surprise three magic missile attacks
sufficed to take her down. marnie made her way through the crowd and
finally reached Tyr's altar, sacrificed the Amulet of Yendor and
ascended to the status of Demigoddess. This after 162192 turns, for a
final score of 7042370. The only voluntary challenge that came up (not
to my surprise) was "You did not wish forany artifact", but, hey,
there's time for playing a harder game!



